	(text "DESIGN NOTES (summary; analysis in docs/stage2/sheet5-architecture-proposal.md rev A1 and sheet5-design-notes.md)\n1. X4 12 V (S5-1/S5-2): U501 TPS259470L. ILIM 2.65-3.36 A; blanking 4.9-15.3 ms; FLT -> X4_PWR_FLT_N -> FPGA switches off (PM-4).\n   FPGA sustained-overload trip 2.75 A / 2 s from the INA226 (PM-5). F501 opens only if U501 fails short.\n2. FAIL-SAFE ENABLE (S5-3/S5-9): Q502 holds EN/UVLO low from +12 V; only X4_PWR_EN high (Q501) releases it. Erased, configuring,\n   reset or unpowered FPGA -> X4 OFF. The FPGA checks for an external source on the X4's USB-C (INA226 VBUS) before enabling (PM-2).\n3. JP501 SERVICE OVERRIDE: 1-2 force OFF; 2-3 force ON bypasses the power manager (bench only, current-limited, X4 USB-C empty; R-57).\n4. 5 V (S5-6): U503 TPS259470L OVLO disconnect 5.53-6.01 V; C513 bounds fast overshoot; U504 TLV76733 survives 18 V.\n5. X4_S0_SENSE is ACTIVE LOW: low = X4 in S0 (S5-5). INA226 at 0x44 (C-28). Every pull-up is on +3V3 (C-29).\n6. GROUND RETURN (S5-8, conditional): H501-H504 bond the X4 standoffs to GND; J502 pin order = X4 J10 (1 GND, 2 +12 V).\n   Zorro power pins stay unconnected. Contact ratings are requirements (R-56). Bench validation B0-B5 before any A2000.\n7. Not yet validated: an ERC-clean result does not imply electrical correctness. No PCB manufacture authorised."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
